Thu Aug 20 08:53:50 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Recreate the package git repo with sha256 object format so it
  matches tree-sitter/_ObsPrj (OBS scmsync was broken: mismatched
  algorithms, client sha256 vs server sha1)
- Switch the python subpackage to the loader binding (same pattern
  as tree-sitter-python):
  * Drop %treesitter_python_build and the C-extension Python
    BuildRequires (devel/installer/pip/setuptools/wheel)
  * Keep %treesitter_python_install: install upstream's
    pure-Python package files and generate a _binding.py that
    loads libtree-sitter-fortran.so, so the parser is not
    compiled a second time
  * Pin Requires: %{name} = %{version}-%{release}
  * Functional %check parses Fortran source through the shim
- New openSUSE:Factory package (Fortran grammar +
  python3-tree-sitter-fortran), needed for python-graphifyy
- Suggests python-tree-sitter >= 0.22 instead of Requires,
  matching tree-sitter-bash, so ring1/product installcheck
  does not demand a non-ring package.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Mon Jul 27 08:36:27 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Initial package of tree-sitter-fortran 0.6.0:
  * Fortran grammar library for the tree-sitter parsing
    framework (libtree-sitter-fortran.so grammar module)
  * Python binding built from the bundled bindings/python as
    pythonXYZ flavor subpackages via the shared
    %treesitter_python_build/_install macros
